constraints:
1 <= M, N <= 10^{5}
0 <= Arr1[i], Arr2[i] <= 10^{6}

expected time complexity: O(M+N)
expected auxiliary space: O(1)

standard_solution_code:
class Solution:

	def maxPathSum(self, arr1, arr2, m, n):
		sum1 = 0
		sum2 = 0
		ans = 0
		(i, j) = (0, 0)
		while i < m or j < n:
			if i == m:
				sum2 += arr2[j]
				j += 1
			elif j == n:
				sum1 += arr1[i]
				i += 1
			elif arr1[i] < arr2[j]:
				sum1 += arr1[i]
				i += 1
			elif arr1[i] > arr2[j]:
				sum2 += arr2[j]
				j += 1
			else:
				ans += max(sum1, sum2) + arr1[i]
				i += 1
				j += 1
				(sum1, sum2) = (0, 0)
		return ans + max(sum1, sum2)
